adjudication.rationale:
In the newly added API route `apps/web/pages/api/webhook/app-credential.ts`, the webhook authentication check directly compares the provided header value to `process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET` using `!==`:

```ts
if (
  req.headers[process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_HEADER_NAME || "calcom-webhook-secret"] !==
  process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET
) {
  return res.status(403).json({ message: "Invalid webhook secret" });
}
```
This is a plain string/byte comparison and is not constant-time, which can introduce a timing side-channel for secret verification endpoints. A constant-time comparison (e.g., `crypto.timingSafeEqual` on Buffers with equal length) is the standard mitigation.
